# Copy to .env.local and fill in only if you need to override defaults.
# .env*.local is gitignored. NOTHING here is required to run the site.
#
# ── Phone-OTP (Firebase Authentication → Phone provider) ─────────────────────
# The Firebase web config is hardcoded in lib/otp.ts because it is PUBLIC by
# design (it ships to the browser regardless). So no env vars are needed — not
# locally and not on Amplify. Security is the Firebase console's "Authorized
# domains" list, not hiding the config. Never put a service-account/private key
# anywhere in the client.
#
# OPTIONAL overrides (only if you point the site at a different Firebase project
# without editing code):
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_API_KEY=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_AUTH_DOMAIN=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_PROJECT_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_STORAGE_BUCKET=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_MESSAGING_SENDER_ID=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_FIREBASE_APP_ID=

# OTP mode — global default, flip without touching code.
#   off  = no OTP step (leads submit as today, no otp tag)
#   soft = OTP shown with "Skip for now"; never blocks; tags otp-verified/unverified
#   hard = OTP required, falls back to otp-unverified after repeated send
#          failures / a timeout (never hard-blocks a lead)
# Per-page overrides live in lib/otp.ts (OTP_MODE_BY_PATH). Defaults to soft.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_OTP_MODE=soft
